  "$mockup_parity_not_verifiable_2026_08_17": {
    "date": "2026-08-17",
    "action": "GAP_RECORDED",
    "question_asked": "Do the dj and loc mockups print the same final structure of styles and visuals as the shipped pages?",
    "answer_for_loc": "UNANSWERABLE AS THE REPO STANDS. Two things are missing at once, and neither can be substituted by inference.",
    "missing_1_no_mockup_in_repo": "21-mockup-field-contract.json audits 'screen/single cpt/location/loc-single-page.html', which lives OUTSIDE the plugins folder and was never copied in. apollo-djs has its counterpart at _sandbox/dj-single-page.mockup.html; apollo-loc has no _sandbox and no mockup. There is no approved artefact here to compare against.",
    "missing_2_no_cell_structure": "apollo-loc never went through the cell treatment. styles/base/single-local.php is a monolith with its per-item context inline at the top (_local_name, address, coords, … from line 31), exactly the shape apollo-djs moved away from. There is no template-parts/single/ tree, no generator, and no render SSOT: apollo_loc_render_single(), apollo_loc_single_context() and apollo_loc_can_view() are all undefined — verified by grep across the whole plugin.",
    "consequence": "The loc surface in includes/surface.php stays correctly DORMANT — apollo_surface_get('loc') returns null, so no REST fragment route is registered and apollo_surface_open_attrs('loc',$id) returns ''. A loc card renders as a plain anchor to /local/{slug}. That is the designed graceful degradation, not a bug.",
    "what_would_make_it_verifiable": [
      "1. Copy the approved loc-single-page.html into apollo-loc/_sandbox/ so the design has a home in the repo, as apollo-djs did.",
      "2. Extract apollo_loc_single_context( int $id ): array out of styles/base/single-local.php; the template extract()s it. Rendered output must not change — that is the whole test.",
      "3. Add apollo_loc_render_single() + apollo_loc_can_view(). The surface, its REST fragment and the lightbox then light up together with no further wiring.",
      "4. Only then does a build-loc-cells.py and a parity assertion have anything to compare."
    ],
    "warning_inherited_from_djs": "When the loc mockup is copied in, check its encoding FIRST. The DJ mockup is character-corrupted (152 lines) while its generated cells are clean — see 09-plugins/apollo-djs.json $mockup_corrupted_generator_disarmed_2026_08_17. If the two mockups travelled together they were likely damaged together.",
    "philosophy_violations_still_open_in_the_loc_mockup": "21-mockup-field-contract.json records VIO-02 (#dockFollow 'Seguir' button with a heart icon), VIO-03 ('Siga o local' copy) and VIO-04 (.map-note printing raw lat/lng plus an internal meta name and the non-existent CPT slug 'events_local' — the real slug is 'local'). These must be fixed in the mockup BEFORE any generator slices it, or the violations become permanent in shipped cells. Copy and icon changes only; no new storage — the fav tables already exist.",
    "risk_if_ignored": "Building loc cells from an unaudited mockup would bake a follow button into production, which 01-philosophy forbids outright (NO_SELECTIVE_FOLLOW, NO_EGO_COUNTERS)."
  }
